        "note": "Prior Lean formalization by Gábor P. Nagy and Attila Vajda of classical Kasami APN and AB theory. It includes Dempwolff-Müller permutation machinery, the Artin-Schreier/MCM treatment of the Kasami derivative, Walsh-moment arguments, and Frobenius transport between complementary exponents. It does not formalize Carlet's cyclic-additive triple-count conjecture or the Fermat-cubic/isogeny completion used in this repository.",
